      "stdout": "text shortcuts.\r\n\r\nAGENT QUICKSTART (driving this as an agent? start here):\r\n  Browse commands:  lyra-cli <domain> --help\r\n\r\nUSAGE:\r\n  lyra-cli <domain> <[subdomain] ...> <action> [--flags] [--options]\r\n\r\n\r\nOPTIONS:\r\n  -h,     --help              Print this help message and exit\r\n  -v,     --version           Show version information and exit.\r\n          --jq TEXT           Pretty-print JSON output; with an optional selector like\r\n                              .result.items[0].id, output the selected JSON value instead of\r\n                              the full schema envelope.\r\n\r\nSUBCOMMANDS:\r\n  translate                   Move a text segment on the canvas.\r\n  content                     Update text content with one atomic shortcut operation.\r\n  effect                      text effect shortcuts.\r\n  wrap-width                  Set a text segment's fixed text-box width (auto-wrap on\r\n                              overflow).\r\n  add                         Add a plain text segment to the draft.\r\n  remove                      Remove a text segment.\r\n                              Alias of `draft segment remove`.\r\n  animation                   text animation shortcuts.\r\n  style                       Update one or more text style parameters in a single command.\r\n                              Fields are routed to their underlying handlers and merged into\r\n                              one patch.\r\n                              Pass a comma-separated --seg-id (e.g. id1,id2,id3) to restyle\r\n                              multiple text segments at once.\r\n\r\nACTION CHAINING\r\n  Shared target:\r\n    lyra-cli draft text [--ref <draft>] <selector> --action <path> <options> ...\r\n  Per-block targets:\r\n    lyra-cli draft text [--ref <draft>] --action <path> <selector> <options> ...\r\n  Public selectors:\r\n    --seg-id, --seg-type, --target-track, --seg-index, --time-window\r\n  Rules:\r\n    Put a shared selector before the first --action.\r\n    Without a shared selector, every action block must declare one.\r\n    Do not mix shared and per-block targets in one chain.\r\n    Shortcut paths use space-separated tokens, for example `filter update`.\r\n    Cross-object chains use `draft --action <object> <path> ...` and per-block targets.\r\n\r\nLEARN MORE\r\n  Use `lyra-cli draft text <subcommand> --help` for a specific shortcut.\r\n",
